.TH UNCOMPRESS "1" "February 2011" "gzip 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gzip \- manual page for uncompress
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uncompress
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,FILE\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uncompress FILEs (by default, in\-place).
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-stdout\fR
write on standard output, keep original files unchanged
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
force overwrite of output file and compress links
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-keep\fR
keep (don't delete) input files
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR
list compressed file contents
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-no\-name\fR
do not save or restore the original name and timestamp
.TP
\fB\-N\fR, \fB\-\-name\fR
save or restore the original name and timestamp
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
suppress all warnings
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-recursive\fR
operate recursively on directories
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-suffix\fR=\fI\,SUF\/\fR
use suffix SUF on compressed files
.HP
\fB\-\-synchronous\fR synchronous output (safer if system crashes, but slower)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-test\fR
test compressed file integrity
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
verbose mode
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
display this help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
display version information and exit
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
